package Patterns;

import java.util.Scanner;

public class Q5 {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Scanner input = new Scanner(System.in);
        System.out.print("Please enter n: ");
        int n = input.nextInt();
        for (int i = 1; i <=n ; i++) {
            for (int j = 0; j <=n-i; j++) {
                System.out.print("* ");

            }
            System.out.println();
        }
    }
}

OUTPUT:
n = 5
* * * * *
* * * *
* * *
* *
*

Approach
Take an integer n as input from the user.
Use an outer loop to iterate through rows from 1 to n.
For each row i, print n - i + 1 stars using an inner loop.
After printing all stars for the current row, move to the next line.
Continue until all rows are printed.

Logic
The outer loop (i) controls the rows.
The inner loop runs n - i + 1 times (j goes from 0 to n - i).
The number of stars decreases by one in each row.

Time Complexity

Total iterations:

n + (n-1) + (n-2) + ... + 1 = n(n + 1)/2

Time Complexity: O(n²)

Space Complexity

Space Complexity: O(1)

